      "reductionNote": "620 checks against values the compiler already types as non-nullable. Most are not dead code; they are the cost of noUncheckedIndexedAccess being off, which types an indexed read as T and so makes the guard after it read as unnecessary. Turning that flag on measures 1,176 errors (verdict in docs/development/lint-and-type-aware-rules.md), so this count falls with that flag, not by editing 620 sites. Lower it opportunistically when a file is already being changed; do not open a sweep. Lowered 274 -> 271 on 2026-08-25 under exactly that rule: the Workflow Flow refactor landed nine new sites in WorkflowFlowNode.svelte, workflow-flow-layout.ts and WorkflowFlowCanvas.test.ts, which held develop's webview lint red. Cleared by making the types honest rather than by deleting guards -- the two source sites annotate the indexed read and the operator lookup as possibly absent, so every runtime guard stands and reads as meaningful -- plus the redundant optional chaining in the test file. Three pre-existing sites in the same test file went with them, which is why the count lands below the old baseline rather than back at it. Host lowered 345 -> 343 across 2026-08-25 under the same rule, two sites in two features: FR-R3-078's `isFencedClaim` discriminates on `'kind' in claim` rather than on a cast plus a comparison the compiler already knows is false; and FR-R3-081's multi-PID sampler takes 'any registered pid' from a loop rather than from `[...keys][0] ?? null`, which with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` off is typed `number` and so reads as dead code to the linter while being load-bearing at runtime. Both made the types honest rather than deleting a guard. Host lowered 343 -> 342 on 2026-08-25 by FR-R3-083, under the same opportunistic rule: extracting the SIGTERM->SIGKILL->confirm ladder out of claude-cli.ts and process-lifecycle-runner.ts into process-tree.ts removed one of two duplicated `.unref?.()` optional calls. The copies had drifted -- one spelled `.unref()` and the other `.unref?.()` -- which is itself an argument for the extraction. No guard was deleted; one of two copies of the same statement stopped existing.",
